  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In an October 2026 statement, Christopher Pilkerton said proposed regulations are designed to address risks from foreign adversaries benefiting from U.S. investment in key technology sectors and would enhance the Outbound Investment Security Program. In 2025 Senate materials, he said vigilance over foreign investment is critical because adversaries seek to undermine U.S. assets, technological competencies, and private data, and that if confirmed he would carefully consider national security risks related to technology advances and ensure CFIUS and the Outbound Investment Security Program are responsive. In a June 2026 reported statement, he asked about the potential weaponization and dual-use implications of technology. In an October 2026 statement, he described the Outbound Investment Security Program as an important tool aimed at addressing the advancement of key technologies by countries of concern that could pose risks to U.S. national security.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s5",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In an October 2026 statement, Christopher Pilkerton said proposed regulations are designed to address risks from foreign adversaries benefiting from U.S. investment in key technology sectors and would enhance the Outbound Investment Security Program.",
     "sids": [
      "s1"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "In 2025 Senate materials, he said vigilance over foreign investment is critical because adversaries seek to undermine U.S. assets, technological competencies, and private data, and that if confirmed he would carefully consider national security risks related to technology advances and ensure CFIUS and the Outbound Investment Security Program are responsive.",
     "sids": [
      "s2",
      "s5"
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "In a June 2026 reported statement, he asked about the potential weaponization and dual-use implications of technology.",
     "sids": [
